      "side": 1,
      "message": "I still believe that keeping the tests close to the library doesn\u0027t fit the rest of EC, although I certainly understand the benefit and am a fan of this, in general. I think the path of least resistance is to simply put the files back into a normal EC file structure, where mock headers are in `include/mock`.\n\nIf this is something we want to do, then it needs to be done all the way. It has been 10 months since you introduced this new pattern. The [comment on the original CL](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/3935025/comment/ac325e94_1cbd5220/) shows the confusion for the code structure and you promised something in a number of weeks. Please try not to use the EC codebase as a staging ground for Zephyr things. Fingerprint still needs EC to work correctly (until we can join in the Zephyr fun).\n\n---\n\nIf you honestly want to support this or **ANY** pattern, then maybe refactor EC to not include all dirs.\n\n```suggestion\ndirs-y +\u003d $(shell find common -type d)\ndirs-y +\u003d $(shell find driver -type d)\n```\n\nThen, maybe add the following to `common/build.mk` to support existing users that only use one layer of directories in driver and common:\n\n```\nincludes-y +\u003d $(shell find common -maxdepth 1 -type d)\n```\n\nAnd for `driver/build.mk`:\n\n```\nincludes-y +\u003d $(shell find driver -maxdepth 1 -type d)\n```\n\nAnd for your own `spi/flash_reg/build.mk`:\n\n```\nincludes-y +\u003d common/spi/flash_reg/public\n```",
